{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-328593" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Hint: One of the eigenvalues of the matrix is ${\\lambda }_{1}=\\text{i}.$*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073450/state.json" "file_sha256" "f73948b84caf4c80e734b125584278683fb0e3a363bae6fe81ee3112cbbd354d"} {"question" "q-328593" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find the eigenvalues and associated eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nWe are given that the eigenvalue is ${\\lambda }_{1}=\\text{i}.$ \n\nLet's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors. For ${\\lambda }_{1}=\\text{i},$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=[\\begin{aligned}-\\text{i} & -1 \\\\ 1 & -\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\text{i} \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvector corresponding to the second eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}$ is \n${v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{1}.$ But we do not require this eigenvector for solving our system.\n\nThe solution that we obtain for the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=\\text{i}$ and its associated eigenvector is\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\text{i}t}.\n$$\n\nWe now express this as a real function. Using Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\text{i}t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}](\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\text{i}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]+\\text{i}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+\\text{i}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${w}_{1}$ and ${w}_{2}$ are linearly independent. Therefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & ={c}_{1}{\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial condition $x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(0) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & =-[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073450/state.json" "file_sha256" "f73948b84caf4c80e734b125584278683fb0e3a363bae6fe81ee3112cbbd354d"} {"question" "q-328593" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073450/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e833b3ccc15aac1e03354d033313cbf9af8e58f7838c2a36bc48cd3827b2a786"} {"question" "q-328593" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073450/state.json" "file_sha256" "f73948b84caf4c80e734b125584278683fb0e3a363bae6fe81ee3112cbbd354d"} {"question" "q-328593" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073450/state.json" "file_sha256" "f73948b84caf4c80e734b125584278683fb0e3a363bae6fe81ee3112cbbd354d"} {"question" "q-328593" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073450/state.json" "file_sha256" "f73948b84caf4c80e734b125584278683fb0e3a363bae6fe81ee3112cbbd354d"} {"question" "q-328599" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Hint: The matrix has the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=2+\\text{i}$ with the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2+\\text{i} \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073450/state.json" "file_sha256" "f73948b84caf4c80e734b125584278683fb0e3a363bae6fe81ee3112cbbd354d"} {"question" "q-328599" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find the eigenvalues and associated eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nWe are given the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=2+\\text{i}$ and the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2+\\text{i} \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvector corresponding to the second eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}$ is \n${v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{1}.$ But we do not require this eigenvector for solving our system.\n\nThe solution that we obtain for the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=2+\\text{i}$ and its associated eigenvector is\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-2+\\text{i} \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]{e}^{(2+\\text{i})t}.\n$$\n\nWe now express this as a real function. Using Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}-2+\\text{i} \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]{e}^{(2+\\text{i})t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2+\\text{i} \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\text{i}(-2{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\text{i}({e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)-{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 5{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\text{i}(5{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\text{i}({e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\ 5{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\text{i}(5{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+\\text{i}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t} \\\\  & ={\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+\\text{i}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${w}_{1}$ and ${w}_{2}$ are linearly independent. Therefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & ={c}_{1}{\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial condition $x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(0) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ 5{c}_{1}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & =\\frac{3}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}-\\frac{4}{5}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073450/state.json" "file_sha256" "f73948b84caf4c80e734b125584278683fb0e3a363bae6fe81ee3112cbbd354d"} {"question" "q-328599" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073450/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e833b3ccc15aac1e03354d033313cbf9af8e58f7838c2a36bc48cd3827b2a786"} {"question" "q-328599" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073450/state.json" "file_sha256" "f73948b84caf4c80e734b125584278683fb0e3a363bae6fe81ee3112cbbd354d"} {"question" "q-328599" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}"] ["math" "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}"] ["math" "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}"] ["math" "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}"] ["math" "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073450/state.json" "file_sha256" "f73948b84caf4c80e734b125584278683fb0e3a363bae6fe81ee3112cbbd354d"} {"question" "q-328599" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073450/state.json" "file_sha256" "f73948b84caf4c80e734b125584278683fb0e3a363bae6fe81ee3112cbbd354d"} {"question" "q-334078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -16 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Hint: One of the eigenvalues of the matrix is ${\\lambda }_{1}=4\\text{i}.$*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073450/state.json" "file_sha256" "f73948b84caf4c80e734b125584278683fb0e3a363bae6fe81ee3112cbbd354d"} {"question" "q-334078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find the eigenvalues and associated eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -16 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nWe are given that the eigenvalue is ${\\lambda }_{1}=4\\text{i}.$ \n\nLet's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors. For ${\\lambda }_{1}=4\\text{i},$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=[\\begin{aligned}-4\\text{i} & 1 \\\\ -16 & -4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & \\text{i} \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}\\text{i} \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvector corresponding to the second eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}$ is \n${v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{1}.$ But we do not require this eigenvector for solving our system.\n\nThe solution that we obtain for the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=4\\text{i}$ and its associated eigenvector is\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\text{i} \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4\\text{i}t}.\n$$\n\nWe now express this as a real function. Using Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\text{i} \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4\\text{i}t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\text{i} \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}](\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\text{i}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)-4\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)-4\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}]+\\text{i}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+\\text{i}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${w}_{1}$ and ${w}_{2}$ are linearly independent. Therefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & ={c}_{1}{\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial condition $x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(0) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{2} \\\\ -4{c}_{1}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & =0[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}]+2[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ -8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073450/state.json" "file_sha256" "f73948b84caf4c80e734b125584278683fb0e3a363bae6fe81ee3112cbbd354d"} {"question" "q-334078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073450/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e833b3ccc15aac1e03354d033313cbf9af8e58f7838c2a36bc48cd3827b2a786"} {"question" "q-334078" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073450/state.json" "file_sha256" "f73948b84caf4c80e734b125584278683fb0e3a363bae6fe81ee3112cbbd354d"} {"question" "q-334078" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ -8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ 16\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+16\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073450/state.json" "file_sha256" "f73948b84caf4c80e734b125584278683fb0e3a363bae6fe81ee3112cbbd354d"} {"question" "q-334078" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ -8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073450/state.json" "file_sha256" "f73948b84caf4c80e734b125584278683fb0e3a363bae6fe81ee3112cbbd354d"} {"question" "q-334113" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 10 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above.\nFind the unknown function $f(t)$ in the general solution to the system, shown below.\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ f(t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}\n$$\n\n*Hint: The matrix has the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=2+3\\text{i}$ with the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1-3\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073450/state.json" "file_sha256" "f73948b84caf4c80e734b125584278683fb0e3a363bae6fe81ee3112cbbd354d"} {"question" "q-334113" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find the eigenvalues and associated eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 10 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nWe are given the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=2+3\\text{i}$ and the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1-3\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvector corresponding to the second eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}$ is \n${v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{1}.$ But we do not require this eigenvector for solving our system.\n\nThe solution that we obtain for the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=2+3\\text{i}$ and its associated eigenvector is\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1-3\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{(2+3\\text{i})t}.\n$$\n\nWe now express this as a real function. Using Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}1-3\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{(2+3\\text{i})t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1-3\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\text{i}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)-3\\text{i}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+3{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\text{i}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t))+\\text{i}{e}^{2t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)) \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\text{i}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+\\text{i}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t} \\\\  & ={\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+\\text{i}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${w}_{1}$ and ${w}_{2}$ are linearly independent. Therefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & ={c}_{1}{\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $f(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073450/state.json" "file_sha256" "f73948b84caf4c80e734b125584278683fb0e3a363bae6fe81ee3112cbbd354d"} {"question" "q-334113" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073450/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e833b3ccc15aac1e03354d033313cbf9af8e58f7838c2a36bc48cd3827b2a786"} {"question" "q-334113" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073450/state.json" "file_sha256" "f73948b84caf4c80e734b125584278683fb0e3a363bae6fe81ee3112cbbd354d"} {"question" "q-334113" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)"] ["math" "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)"] ["math" "10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)"] ["math" "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073450/state.json" "file_sha256" "f73948b84caf4c80e734b125584278683fb0e3a363bae6fe81ee3112cbbd354d"} {"question" "q-334113" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073450/state.json" "file_sha256" "f73948b84caf4c80e734b125584278683fb0e3a363bae6fe81ee3112cbbd354d"} {"question" "q-334221" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -6\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Hint: The matrix has the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=-4+\\text{i}$ with the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2+\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073450/state.json" "file_sha256" "f73948b84caf4c80e734b125584278683fb0e3a363bae6fe81ee3112cbbd354d"} {"question" "q-334221" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find the eigenvalues and associated eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -6\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nWe are given the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=-4+\\text{i}$ and the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2+\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvector corresponding to the second eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}$ is \n${v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{1}.$ But we do not require this eigenvector for solving our system.\n\nThe solution that we obtain for the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=-4+\\text{i}$ and its associated eigenvector is\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2+\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{(-4+\\text{i})t}.\n$$\n\nWe now express this as a real function. Using Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}2+\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{(-4+\\text{i})t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2+\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{-4t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2\\text{i}{e}^{-4t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\text{i}{e}^{-4t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{-4t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ {e}^{-4t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\text{i}{e}^{-4t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t}+\\text{i}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t} \\\\  & ={\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+\\text{i}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${w}_{1}$ and ${w}_{2}$ are linearly independent. Therefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & ={c}_{1}{\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial condition $x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(0) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & =-[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t}+3[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+7\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073450/state.json" "file_sha256" "f73948b84caf4c80e734b125584278683fb0e3a363bae6fe81ee3112cbbd354d"} {"question" "q-334221" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073450/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e833b3ccc15aac1e03354d033313cbf9af8e58f7838c2a36bc48cd3827b2a786"} {"question" "q-334221" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073450/state.json" "file_sha256" "f73948b84caf4c80e734b125584278683fb0e3a363bae6fe81ee3112cbbd354d"} {"question" "q-334221" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t}"] ["math" "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t}"] ["math" "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+7\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t}"] ["math" "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t}"] ["math" "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073450/state.json" "file_sha256" "f73948b84caf4c80e734b125584278683fb0e3a363bae6fe81ee3112cbbd354d"} {"question